WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.180
Numbers tell the story, so let's learn to shape them.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.911
In this lesson, you will learn to summarize a column with Statistics, calculate with

3
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:10.939
the Standard tools, and round values.

4
00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:17.360
You will also learn when to change a column and when to add a new one. Let's dive in!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.759
We are in Power Query with the Financial Sample table.

6
00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:31.340
Select a number column, and the Transform tab lights up with Statistics, Standard, Scientific, Trigonometry, and Rounding.

7
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.453
Statistics gives you one summary value for the whole column:

8
00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:49.640
the sum, minimum, maximum, median, average, or standard deviation.

9
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.358
But first, take a moment to scroll and understand each column:

10
00:01:01.358 --> 00:01:04.674
segment, country, product, discount band, and units sold.

11
00:01:04.674 --> 00:01:07.160
Knowing your data always pays off.

12
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.731
Here I chose Standard Deviation on Units Sold.

13
00:01:25.731 --> 00:01:29.394
The answer is about eight hundred sixty seven. But notice:

14
00:01:29.394 --> 00:01:33.057
Power Query replaced the whole table with this one number!

15
00:01:33.057 --> 00:01:36.720
So we remove that step, and the table comes back.

16
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.357
Next, the Standard menu.

17
00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:55.419
Add, Multiply, Subtract, Divide, and Percent Of change every value in the column.

18
00:01:55.419 --> 00:02:00.480
Add, for example, asks for a number and adds it to each row.

19
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.500
Here is a key tip.

20
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.900
On the Transform tab, these tools change the column itself.

21
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.660
On the Add Column tab, they create a new column and keep the original.

22
00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.060
When you still need the raw values, add a column.

23
00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.505
Finally, Rounding.

24
00:02:49.505 --> 00:02:54.437
Round Up goes to the next whole number, Round Down to the one before,

25
00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:57.255
and Round lets you choose the decimal places.

26
00:02:57.255 --> 00:03:00.074
Every change becomes a step you can undo.

27
00:03:00.074 --> 00:03:02.540
Now try it with your own data!

